  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-124528",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We wish to express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{125}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta =-{125}^{∘}.$\n\nTo express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{125}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1**: Find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$ We do this by adding integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get our desired angle:\n\n$$\n-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={235}^{∘}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{125}^{∘})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({235}^{∘}).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266661/assets/e31971d4c2c3837953a9f9090657c4143a1624ff8572684ea9ab9539ef5fe913.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Compute the reference angle. Since $\\theta ={235}^{∘}$ is in the $3$rd quadrant, the reference angle is\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}={235}^{∘}-{180}^{∘}={55}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 3**: Determine the correct sign. The tangent function is positive $(+)$ in the third quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{125}^{∘})=+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({55}^{∘})\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{125}^{∘})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({55}^{∘}).\n$$",
